# Same client resolution (Farm + Watch)

`ProjectD2-Realm` (Farm) and `ProjectD2-Watch` (Watch) must use the **same** `ddraw.ini` / launcher `width` and `height`.

## Why

AutoSkill UI clicks (`Config.AutoSkill.UIClick`), F9 calibration, and other screen/window coord scripts break if resolution differs between clients.

## Current shared size

- `width=1068`
- `height=600`

(Change both folders together if you ever resize.)

## Hard rules

- Never shrink Farm resolution for “performance” while leaving Watch larger (or vice versa).
- When editing `ddraw.ini` or `AppData\launcherSettings.json` DdrawOptions, keep `Width`/`Height` identical across Realm and Watch.
- Lean Farm via `maxfps`, empty `shader`, `-sleepy` — **not** via a different resolution.
- Never use `-ns` on Farm/Watch profiles here — it crashes this PD2 client stack.
